>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CS_INST_STEP_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.CS_INST_STEP_TAC : clasetLib.claset -> NTactical.ntactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constructs a claset-explicit, instantiating one-step tactic.

`CS_INST_STEP_TAC cs` tries unifying assumption, contradiction, zero-premise
safe rules and positive-premise safe rules on the first goal. It performs
no preliminary safe saturation, applies no wrappers, and tries no unsafe
rules. Each result is replayed and may contain residual goals.

Unlike `INST_STEP_TAC`, this interface uses a prepared rule set, exposes
its alternative result sequence, and processes no theorem-list markers.

### Failure

Produces no result if no unifying assumption, contradiction or safe rule
applies. Replay failure is reported as an error.

### Example

``` hol4
val inst_step =
  classicalLib.CS_INST_STEP_TAC (clasetLib.the_claset ());
```

